1:  1f5e6e4 = 1:  1f5e6e4 inputs: pin network availability vpsAdmin revision
2:  d0b4f40 ! 2:  ce2c8cd runtime: add portable KB launcher and capture leases
    @@ Commit message
     
         Accept the selected server's saved null or false non-primary association
         while retaining literal false requests and strictly false pickability flags.
    -    Model its save callback and reject malformed flags before address creation
    -    or network disable.
    +    Model its save callback and reject malformed flags before address creation.
    +
    +    Keep the ordinary IP-list fixture on enabled networks. Validate retained
    +    pools before association or address writes, preserve owned registration and
    +    read-only reruns, and refuse incompatible old fixture identities. The capture
    +    shows the assigned and detached addresses needed by member documentation.
     
      ## .github/workflows/check.yml ##
     @@ .github/workflows/check.yml: on:
    @@ README.md: implementations.
     +The `networking/ip-address-list` checkpoint instead uses the `ip-inventory`
     +fixture: one real VPS with 1 CPU, 1024 MiB RAM and 4096 MiB disk, its enabled
     +assigned address, and an owned detached address from a dedicated documentation
    -+pool. The fixture provisions that address while the pool is enabled, then
    -+disables only that pool. Reruns validate the same allocation without enabling
    -+the pool or charging again. Other checkpoints retain their full fixtures and
    -+the primary address pools remain enabled.
    ++pool. Both pools remain enabled. Reruns validate the same allocation without
    ++changing network availability or charging again. Other checkpoints retain
    ++their full fixtures.
     +
     +This fixture requires explicit `test-admin` (level 99), `test-user1` and
     +`test-user2` (both level 1) entries in the dedicated configuration's `seed.users`.
    @@ cluster/runtime-contract.md (new)
     +
     +The bilingual phase selects only `networking/ip-address-list` and its
